Tech2Wild/Kai (tonyd2wild)
  https://github.com/tonyd2wild/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-vLLM-DGX-Spark (MIT, licenses/Tech2Wild-MIT.txt)
  The four-Spark TP4 recipe: disk-backed Engram tables and their staging before the forward
  (CUDA graphs), node-local Engram rows, SM12x page-size and indexer fixes, the image build
  and prewarm approach, the relaunch order, the hang check and the GPU clock-latch check.
  - patches/*/01..07-tony-*.diff are diffs of their patch files (commit fc725ecf) against vLLM;
    patches/measured-odirect/04-tony-mtxc-engram-odirect.diff adds this repo's O_DIRECT read path
  - bench/tony/v41bench.py, v41needle.py, prompts-v1.json are vendored unmodified
  - build/stable-extension.sh, Dockerfile.runtime, prewarm.py, verify-runtime.py,
    ops/hangcheck.sh, ops/gpu-burn.sh and the Engram slice format derive from their scripts
  - patches/exl3-tp3e names and hashes their EXL3 lane patch set tp3e (commit fc725ecf); the
    files are fetched from their repository at render time, not copied here

bot-lab-21
  https://huggingface.co/bot-lab-21/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-EXL3-3.5bpw-Pollard
  The EXL3 3.5 bpw checkpoint of the routed experts and the cuda-exl3 config.py / moe.py that
  tp3e carries. weights/manifest-exl3-f129e31a.tsv lists that revision's file hashes; nothing
  of it is redistributed here. cuda-exl3 itself is Zeuss5/cuda-exl3, built at 6a1ffc34.

0xTank
  https://huggingface.co/0xTank/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-vLLM-4x-GB10-Recipe (Apache-2.0 and MIT)
  The measured 600K/K3 configuration this recipe reproduces, the vLLM 172d9a17 pin, the
  graph startup-state fix and the compact MXFP8 output-projection decode kernel.
  - patches/*/08..10-0xtank-*.diff and patches/new/compact_o_proj.py
  - launch/node.sh follows their parameterized launcher

vLLM contributors (Apache-2.0)
  Every patched file is a vLLM module; the diffs apply to vllm-project/vllm at
  172d9a17117219952fd3d4cdbb04ecb2a09163f4 and the per-file SPDX headers remain.

MiaAI-Lab (AGPL-3.0), https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-DGX-Sparks
  Ideas only, no code: O_DIRECT Engram reads, NCCL buffer sizing, the b12x MXFP8 dense route
